  "source": "Sanitized from read-only production Loki queries and bounded Docker log tails",
  "notes": [
    "Identifiers, addresses, users, URLs, and tokens were replaced with reserved or obvious fixture values.",
    "Airflow ERROR and CRITICAL are shape-preserving variants of the observed production bracketed format because neither occurred in the sampled seven-day Loki window.",
    "The gunicorn supervisor and {file.py:line} task-logger cases are upstream default formats, not lines observed in that window; they exist because those are the shapes the parser most needs to catch and the sample could not supply. Stage 4 confirms them against real output.",
    "oauth_lifecycle_severity_wins_over_status is synthetic: it is a single line matching both oauth patterns, and it exists only to pin which of the two sets the level.",
    "Traceback continuation lines are intentionally excluded; the initiating bracketed ERROR or CRITICAL record is retained.",
    "Every container_stdout case here was replayed through grafana/promtail:3.5.8 with -dry-run -stdin against this repository's pipeline stages; the retained set and labels below are what Go produced.",
    "Plan 154 Stage B added the postgres and trawl cases. Every postgres line except postgres_panic_constructed is a verbatim production capture. No WARNING occurred naturally in the twenty days of log available on 2026-09-07, so one was induced on 2026-09-08 with `BEGIN; BEGIN; ROLLBACK;` -- which writes nothing -- rather than fabricated. PANIC cannot be induced without crashing the server, so it stays a shape-preserving construction; POSTGRES_LEVEL_MAP would otherwise have an untested branch.",
    "trawl_tab_space_fallback_stays_info pins a decision rather than a parse: the fallback fires only after the primary solve method failed, and it is deliberately INFO so it cannot make WARNING trawl's routine level. Plan 155 Stage 0 item 4 holds the reasoning and the escalation rule that replaces it."
